cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "android-llm-bench: running AI language models on an Android phone (OnePlus Nord 2), and what limits the speed"
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Prashant
    family-names: Singh
date-released: 2026-10-28
version: "1.0"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - llm
  - on-device inference
  - llama.cpp
  - android
  - benchmark
  - quantization
  - memory bandwidth
  - thermal throttling
abstract: >-
  Six versions of the Qwen3.5 language model (0.8B, 2B and 4B parameters, each
  at 4-bit and 8-bit) were run offline with llama.cpp on a OnePlus Nord 2
  (MediaTek Dimensity 1200, 8 GB RAM). Writing speed followed memory bandwidth
  divided by model size, at 57-78% of the 34.1 GB/s limit. Sustained work halved
  the speed once the battery reached 40 degrees C. The 4B 4-bit model gave the
  best answers (19 of 20) at about 7 tokens per second.
